#Figure 2

Data tables and scripts used to generate images for Figure 2

For Figure 2d, the length of each assigned chromosome and total genome sequence length for all chromosome-level assemblies on GenBank was taken from the sequence-report file.

For Figure 2e, compleasm was run using the vertebrata_odb12 database on each "primary" vertebrate genome assembly for each specimen in GenBank. The contig N50 statistic was taken from the assembly report for each assembly directly using ncbi-datasets.

For Figure 2f, the contig and scaffold statistics were generated by splitting the assembly into contigs at Ns and then running `samtools faidx` on the raw assembly file (scaffolds) or split file (contigs). The `get_nx.py` script then bins these values into 1,000 bins per genome to be able to average across all genomes for each lineage in the R script.
